for people in parts of the US this  Christmas is beginning to look a lot  like their coldest in decades more than  90 million in at least 37 states have  been warned off severe winter weather  the Arctic blast began in the Pacific  Northwest and has swept East causing  temperatures to plunge across the U.S  and Canada the wintry conditions and  freezing roads have brought travel chaos  and also misery for many stranded at  airports at the start of the busiest  travel time of the year  checked our flight you know five this  morning and headed to the airport and  then when we got here we found it was  canceled tired stressed hungry  just hopeless honestly  about 80 percent of the US is set to  experience Sub-Zero temperatures  including places as far south as Texas  the governors of Kentucky and North  Carolina have declared states of  emergency  and while people in some areas are used  to conditions like these many have never  seen such extremely cold weather in a  long time I think in my seven and a half  years living in the Pacific Northwest  and and specifically here in monologue  County area I don't remember a specific  instance where I can remember  temperatures quite this low as the storm  develops it's set to become what U.S  meteorologists call a bomb Cyclone  that's when a system intensifies rapidly  with its central air pressure dropping  at least 24 millibars in 24 hours that  would put it in line with the pressure  of a category three hurricane and bring  about blizzards as well as severe  thunderstorms and whiteout conditions  the once in a generation winter weather  event is threatening to deliver the  coldest Christmas to the Midwest in  nearly 40 years and it may not be so  long until the next one U.S scientists  say climate change has made storms like  this increasing frequency and intensity  during the past 70 years caroleg Al  Jazeera
 

